  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, PCA → 48.5% acc), leaving almost all design dimensions unexplored. The most fundamental uncertainty is whether the image modality carries discriminative signal at all. Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest unimodal baseline for the image side, structurally parallel to config_001 (singleprofile, no aggregation, no fusion). If image-only performs competitively with or above the RNA baseline, it justifies investing subsequent experiments in multimodal fusion and aggregation. If it performs poorly, we can redirect the budget toward RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. This experiment isolates the image modality's standalone contribution without confounding it with fusion strategy or multiprofile complexity, making it the highest-information-gain choice under a tight budget."
}

